    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000064">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000219"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A pregnancy, neonatal and perinatal AE that displays a disorder associated with pregnancy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>prenatal AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complications_of_pregnancy</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prenatal_diagnosis</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <dc:creator>YH, JX</dc:creator>
        <rdfs:label>pregnancy AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000066 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000066">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000040"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a procedure complication AE that occurs after a surgery.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>surgery AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>surgery adverse event</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>surgical procedure AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>The key difference between a surgery and a procedure is the need for an incision. Making an incision, or cutting into the skin to gain access to the body’s deeper tissues or organs, is a defining characteristic of surgery. Technically speaking, a surgery is a specific type of procedure. A procedure is a broad general term that refers to any series of pre-defined steps that should be followed to achieve a desired result. Therefore, a “surgical procedure” is synonymous with a “surgery.”  See more: http://www.wisegeekhealth.com/what-is-the-difference-between-a-surgery-and-a-procedure.htm.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>surgery adverse event</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000068 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000068">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000098"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sugery adverse event that has an outcome of pressure ulcer.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>surgery-induced bedsore AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>surgery-induced decubitus ulcer AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label>surgery-induced pressure ulcer AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000069 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000069">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">an adverse event which occurs in a metabolism process (including anabolism and catabolism), endocrine system, or exocrine system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SS, YH, JX</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>metabolism, endocrine, and exocrine system AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10027433</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">metabolism, endocrine or exocrine system AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>MP: 0005266</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


