    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000388 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000388">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000582"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sensory capability AE that has an outcome of dizziness</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10013573</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Dizziness describes a number of subjective symptoms, which the patient may describe as feelings of lightheadedness, floating, wooziness, giddiness, confusion, disorientation or loss of balance. Medical terms include vertigo, disequilibrium, pre-syncope or syncoptic episode. Causes may stem from a variety of failures of equilibrioception, hypotension, cerebral hypoxia or a reaction to environmental chemicals or drugs.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>dizziness AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE:E12631</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002321</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt:C37943</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0012833</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000389 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000389">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000556"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>peripheral edema AE is an edema AE that results in swelling of tissues, usually in the lower limbs, due to the accumulation of fluids</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>edema peripheral AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>oedema peripheral AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>peripheral edema AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peripheral_edema</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10030124</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10050068</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>edema limbs AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E11086</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C78262</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000390 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000390">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000582"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sensory capability AE that has an outcome of malaise</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10025482</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Malaise is a feeling of general discomfort or uneasiness, an &quot;out of sorts&quot; feeling. Malaise is often the first indication of an infection or other disease. Vaccination may induce malaise.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>malaise AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E11152</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002321</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C3832</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0231218</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000391 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000391">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavior and neurological AE that has an outcome of somnolence</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>drowsiness</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10041349</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Somnolence (or &quot;drowsiness&quot;) is a state of near-sleep, a strong desire for sleep, or sleeping for unusually long periods (c.f. hypersomnia).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>somnolence AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE:E12814</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001262</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt:C26754</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C2830004</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000392 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000392">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000162"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sensory neuropathy AE that shows a sensation of tingling, pricking, or numbness of a person&apos;s skin with no apparent long-term physical effect.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>paraesthesia AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paraesthesia</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10033775</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10033987</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Paresthesia is more generally known as the feeling of &quot;pins and needles&quot; or of a limb being &quot;asleep&quot; (although this is not directly related to the phenomenon of sleep). The manifestation of paresthesia may be transient or chronic.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>paresthesia AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E12758</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C28177</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000393 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000393">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavior and neurological AE that has an outcome of abnormal crying in a patient</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10011469</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>crying abnormal AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000394 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000394">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000582"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sensory capability AE that has an outcome of chills</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>feeling cold AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10008531</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Chills refers to feeling cold after an exposure to a cold environment. The word can also refer to an episode of shivering, accompanied by paleness and feeling cold.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>chills AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E11074</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001945</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C35143</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0085593</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000395 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000395">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavior and neurological AE that has an outcome of stupor</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10042264</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Stupor is the lack of critical cognitive function and level of consciousness wherein a sufferer is almost entirely unresponsive and only responds to base stimuli such as pain. The word derives from the Latin stupure, meaning insensible. Being characterised by impairments of reactions to external stimuli, in this case, vaccine immunization.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>stupor AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0004372</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0085628</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000396 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000396">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000574"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a gustatory system AE which demonstrates a decreased sensation of appetite.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>anorexia nervosa AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>decreased appetite AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/anorexia/basics/definition/con-20033002</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849 xml:lang="en">厌食症</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10002646</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10002649</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10061428</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>anorexia AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E12252</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002039</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C2875</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0003123</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000397 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000397">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000556"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>face edema AE is an edema AE that results in facial swelling, the build-up of fluid in the tissues of the face. Swelling may also affect the neck and upper arms</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>emema face AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>face oedema AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>oedema face AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB:http://www.nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/ency/article/003105.htm</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>swelling face</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10014222</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10016029</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10042682</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>face edema AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E11082</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C78289</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000398 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000398">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000571"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an abnormal respiration AE that shows a sudden and often repetitively occurring reflex to keep the throat and airways clear</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>coughing AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/cough</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/cough.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0003232>cough</obo:OAE_0003232>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10011224</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>cough AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE:E13364</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt:C37935</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


