    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000405 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000405">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000333"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a muscular weakness AE that has an outcome of myasthenia. Myasthenia represenats myasthenia gravis, a neuromuscular disease leading to fluctuating muscle weakness and fatiguability.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>myasthenia gravis</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>myasthenia syndrome AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>myasthenic syndrome AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label>myasthenia AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001324</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0947912</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000406 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000406">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000374"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a pain AE that occurs at the chest</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;chest pain&apos; was mentioned in 1,752 VAERS reports (1.4%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10008479</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>chest pain AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001681</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0008031</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000407 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000407">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000162"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sensory neuropathy AE which has an outcome of sensory axonal characterized by damage to axonas of the peripheral nervous system (PNS)</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>AG, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>sensory axonal AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000409 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000409">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000581"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a movement disorder AE that has an outcome of twitching, an involuntary sudden movement of part of the body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;twitching&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 1,511 VAERS reports (1.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>twitching AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000410 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000410">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000579"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a seizure AE that has an outcome of a seizure disorder associated with an elevated temperature</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, BY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1176205-overview</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label>febrile seizure AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000411 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000411">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000378"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a respiratory system AE which has an outcome of asthma</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>哮喘</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10003553</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Asthma is a common chronic lung disease. It has been defined by the National Heart, Lung and Blood Institute as a common chronic disorder of the airways that is complex and characterized by variable and recurring symptoms, airflow obstruction, bronchial hyperresponsiveness (bronchospasm), and an underlying inflammation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>asthma AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002099</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0004096</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000412 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000412">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000374"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a pain AE that has an outcome of neck pain</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;neck pain&apos; was mentioned in 1,323 VAERS reports (1.0%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10028836</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>neck pain AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E12493</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0003418</rdfs:seeAlso>
