        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0015397</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000444 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000444">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavior and neurological AE that has an outcome of autism</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>Autism is a brain development disorder characterized by impaired social interaction and communication, and by restricted and repetitive behavior.</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label>autism AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000445 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000445">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000588"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a hematopoietic system AE which has an outcome of sedimentation rate increased</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;sedimentation rate increased&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 530 VAERS reports (0.4%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>This term should be inferred to lab test abnormal.</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>ESR</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>erythrocyte sedimentation rate</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>red blood cell sedimentation rate increased AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>sedrate</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>Sedimentation rate is a diagnostic test for inflammation. The test measures the rate at which red blood cells fall to the bottom of a tube over time. An increased sedimentation rate corresponds to increased non-specific inflammation in the body. It is often called &quot;sedrate&quot; for short.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>red blood cell sedimentation rate increased AE is an AE: sedimentation rate increased that has an increase in rate at which red blood cells precipitate in a period of 1 hour.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>sedimentation rate increased AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000446 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000446">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000596"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an arthritis AE that has an outcome of arthritis due to an infection in another part of the body</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>DJ, SS, YH, DA</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>reactive arthritis AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>reiter&apos;s syndrome AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16822921</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2563769/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18436339</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">10038294</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10003267</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>arthritis reactive AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000447 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000447">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000578"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an abnormal vision AE which has an outcome of amblyopia</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10001906</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>amblyopia AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0000646</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0002418</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000448 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000448">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001797"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a psychiatric disorder AE that has an outcome of mental retardation</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>mental retardation AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001249</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0025362</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000449 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000449">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000362"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a rash AE which shows red, target-shaped or &quot;bulls-eye&quot; patches or sores on the skin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://kidshealth.org/parent/infections/skin/erythema_multiforme.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythema_multiforme</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10015218</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>The erythema multiforme rash usually begins on the arms, hands, legs, and feet, but you might also find it on the face, neck, and body. It also can affect the lips and inside the mouth. It usuallys follows an infection or drug exposure.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>erythema multiforme AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE:E13627</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0010783</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt:C3024</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0014742</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000450 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000450">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001694"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a lab test abnormal AE that has an outcome of SGOT increased</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;SGOT increased&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 477 VAERS reports (0.4%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>SGOT respresents serum glutamic oxaloacetic transaminase, an enzyme that is normally present in liver and heart cells. SGOT is released into blood when the liver or heart is damaged. The blood SGOT levels are thus elevated with liver damage (for example, from viral hepatitis) or with an insult to the heart (for example, from a heart attack). Some medications can also raise SGOT levels. SGOT is also called aspartate aminotransferase (AST).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>SGOT increased AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000451 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000451">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001694"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a lab test abnormal AE that has an outcome of SGPT increased</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;SGPT increased&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 459 VAERS reports (0.4%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>SGPT represents serum glutamic pyruvic transaminase, an enzyme that is normally present in liver and heart cells. SGPT is released into blood when the liver or heart are damaged. The blood SGPT levels are thus elevated with liver damage (for example, from viral hepatitis) or with an insult to the heart (for example, from a heart attack). Some medications can also raise SGPT levels. SGPT is also called alanine aminotransferase (ALT).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>SGPT increased AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000452 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000452">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavioral and neurological AE that has an outcome of thinking abnormality</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;thinking abnormality&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 457 VAERS reports (0.4%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, JX</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10043431</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>thinking abnormality AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000453 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000453">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000554"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an abnormal digestion AE which has an outcome of dyspepsia</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;dyspepsia&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 454 VAERS reports (0.4%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10013946</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Dyspepsia is popularly known as indigestion, meaning hard or difficult digestion. It is a medical condition characterized by chronic or recurrent pain in the upper abdomen, upper abdominal fullness and feeling full earlier than expected when eating.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>dyspepsia AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal">CTCAE: E10617</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Literal">NCIt: C26756</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002577</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0013395</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000454 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000454">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000568"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an allergy AE which has an outcome of anaphylactoid reaction AE is an acute systemic (multi-system) and very severe Type I Hypersensitivity allergic reaction in humans and other mammals. Minute amounts of allergens may cause a life-threatening anaphylactic reaction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;anaphylactoid reaction&apos; was mentioned in 452 VAERS reports (0.4%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22293078</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10002198</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10002216</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>anaphylactoid reaction AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0100845</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0340865</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000455 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000455">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000439"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a digestive system AE which has an outcome of a gastrointestinal disorder</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;gastrointestinal disorder&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 449 VAERS reports (0.3%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>gastrointestinal disorder AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0011024</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0017178</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000456 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000456">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000556"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an edema AE that has an outcome of accumulation of fluid in the peritoneal cavity</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>DJ, SS, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23296107</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10003445</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>ascites AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E10502</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001541</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C2885</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0003962</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000457 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000457">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000584"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a hypersensitivity AE which has an outcome of serum sickness</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;serum sickness&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 428 VAERS reports (0.3%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10040400</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Serum sickness is a reaction to proteins in antiserum derived from an animal source. It is a type of hypersensitivity, specifically immune complex hypersensitivity (type III).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>serum sickness AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E11276</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C79718</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000458 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000458">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000366"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000469"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an abscess AE which has an outcome of injection-site abscess</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>injection-site abscess AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000459 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000459">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001643"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a neurological, special senses and psychiatric investigation result abnormal AE that is the abnormal result of a procedure that uses small, flat metal discs (electrodes) attached to your scalp to detect electrical activity in your brain</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;abnormal electroencephalogram&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 420 VAERS reports (0.3%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, EB</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.mayoclinic.com/health/eeg/MY00296</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10000130</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>abnormal electroencephalogram result AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000460 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000460">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000388"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a dizziness AE that has an outcome of vertigo</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;vertigo&apos; was mentioned in 412 VAERS reports (0.3%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10047340</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Vertigo is a specific type of dizziness, a major symptom of a balance disorder. It is the sensation of spinning or swaying while the body is actually stationary with respect to the surroundings. The effects of vertigo may be slight. It can cause nausea and vomiting and, in severe cases, it may give rise to difficulties with standing and walking.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>vertigo AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E10291</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002321</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C38057</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0042571</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000461 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000461">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000084"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a cardiac disorder AE that has an outcome of heartarrest, the abrupt cessation of normal circulation of the blood due to failure of the heart to contract effectively during systole.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>cardiopulmonary arrest</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>circulatory arrest</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>heart arrest AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myocardial_infarction</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/cardiac+arrest</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10007515</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10007617</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10028596</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>cardiac arrest</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E10101</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIT: C50479</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000462 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000462">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000564"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a respiratory system inflammation AE which has an outcome of bronchitis</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>Bronchitis is an inflammation of the air passages within the lungs. It occurs when the trachea (windpipe) and the large and small bronchi (airways) within the lungs become inflamed because of infection or other causes.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>bronchitis AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002837</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0006277</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000463 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000463">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000579"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a seizure AE that has an outcome of grand malconvulsion</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>A generalized seizure disorder characterized by recurrent major motor seizures. The initial brief tonic phase is marked by trunk flexion followed by diffuse extension of the trunk and extremities. The clonic phase features rhythmic flexor contractions of the trunk and limbs, pupillary dilation, elevations of blood pressure and pulse, urinary incontinence, and tongue biting. This is followed by a profound state of depressed consciousness (post-ictal state) which gradually improves over minutes to hours. The disorder may be cryptogenic, familial, or symptomatic (caused by an identified disease process).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>grand malconvulsion AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000464 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000464">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001694"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a liver related investigation result abnormal AE which shows an abnormal test result in a liver function test, indicating aberrant function of liver.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;liver function tests abnormal&apos; was mentioned in 717 VAERS reports (0.6%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/hepatic+function</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10019670</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10024690</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>liver function test abnormal AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>MP: MP_0000609</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000465 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000465">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an AE that occurs in ear.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>ear disorder AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label>ear  AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0000598</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0013447</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000466 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000466">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000363"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an infection AE that results in detrimental colonization of a host organism by virus</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>viral infection</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viral_infection</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label>viral infection AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0005364</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0042769</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000467 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000467">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000581"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a movement disorder AE that has an outcome of lacrimation disorder</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;lacrimation disorder&apos; was mentioned in 334 VAERS reports (0.3%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>Lacrimation is the production, secretion, and shedding of tears.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>lacrimation disorder AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000468 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000468">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001135"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a liver/biliary system AE which has an outcome of jaundice, which is the clinical manifestation of hyperbilirubinemia, with deposition of bile pigments in the skin, resulting in yellowish staining of the skin and mucous membranes</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;jaundice&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 317 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SS, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>icterus AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaundice</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10023126</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>jaundice AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0000952</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>MP: MP_0000611</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0022346</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000469 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000469">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an immune system disorder AE which shows an enclosed collection of liquefied tissue, known as pus, somewhere in the body. Abscess is the result of the body&apos;s defensive reaction to foreign material.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>abscessus</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/abscess</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10000269</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>An abscess is a collection of pus (dead neutrophils) that has accumulated in a cavity formed by the tissue on the basis of an infectious process (usually caused by bacteria or parasites) or other foreign materials (e.g. splinters, bullet wounds, or injecting needles). It is a defensive reaction of the tissue to prevent the spread of infectious materials to other parts of the body.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>abscess AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002722</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0000833</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000470 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000470">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000374"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a pain AE that has an outcome of eye pain</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS),  &apos;eye pain&apos; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 316 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10015958</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>eye pain AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E10376</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0200025</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C78287</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0151827</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000471 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000471">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000582"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sensory capability AE that has an outcome of palpitation</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palpitations</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10033557</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>A palpitation is an abnormal awareness of the beating of the heart, whether it is too slow, too fast, irregular, or at its normal frequency.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>palpitation AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000472 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000472">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000556"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an edema AE which has an outcome of tongue edema</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, RR</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>tongue oedema AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>tongue swelling AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.medterms.com/script/main/art.asp?articlekey=97582</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10042727</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>tongue edema AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000473 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000473">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000374"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a pain AE that has an outcome of ear pain</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;ear pain&apos; was mentioned in 302 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10014020</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>ear pain AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E10262</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0010833</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C37944</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0013456</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000474 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000474">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000556"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an edema AE which has an outcome of angioedema</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SJ</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>angioneurotic edema </obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/hives-and-angioedema/basics/definition/con-20014815
</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10002473</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Angioedema is the rapid swelling (edema) of the dermis, subcutaneous tissue, mucosa and submucosal tissues often around the eyes and lips. It is very similar to urticaria, but urticaria, commonly known as hives, occurs in the upper dermis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>angioedema AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000475 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000475">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000596"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An arthritis AE that has the outcome of rheumatoid arthritis. Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune disease that causes chronic inflammation of the joints and may also cause inflammation of the tissue around the joints, as well as other organs in the body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>rheumatoid arthritis AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0005681</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0003873</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000476 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000476">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an AE that occurs in immune system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;immune system disorder&apos; was mentioned in 292 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>immune system disorder AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label>immune system AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002715</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0021053</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000477 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000477">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an immune system disorder AE which has an outcome of antinuclear antibody present</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;antinuclear antibody present&apos;; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 288 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>anti-nuclear factor present</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>The presence of anti-nuclear antibodies (ANAs) that are antibodies directed against contents of the cell nucleus. ANAs are present in higher than normal numbers in autoimmune disease. The ANA test measures the pattern and amount of autoantibody which can attack the body&apos;s tissues as if they were foreign material. Autoantibodies are present in low titers in the general population, but in about 5% of the population, their concentration is increased, and about half of this 5% have an autoimmune disease.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>antinuclear antibody present AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000478 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000478">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000570"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a nervous system AE which involves inflammation of the spinal cord, which disrupts central nervous system functions linking the brain and limbs.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10028524</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>myelitis AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E12732</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C26832</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000479 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000479">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000377"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a headache AE that has an outcome of migraine</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;migraine&apos;; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 267 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>migraine headache</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>A migraine is a very painful type of headache. People who get migraines often describe the pain as pulsing or throbbing in one area of the head. During migraines, people are very sensitive to light and sound. They may also become nauseated and vomit.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>migraine AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002076</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0149931</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000480 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000480">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000487"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Thrombocytopenic purpura AE are purpura AE associated with a reduction in circulating blood platelets which can result from a variety of causes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;thrombocytopenic purpura&apos;; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 267 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10043561</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>thrombocytopenic purpura AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0004829</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0857305</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000481 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000481">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>multiple sclerosis AE is an immune system disorder AE, or an autoimmune condition in which the immune system attacks the central nervous system, leading to demyelination.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>MS</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>disseminated sclerosis</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>encephalomyelitis disseminata</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10028245</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>multiple sclerosis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000482 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000482">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavior and neurological AE that has an outcome of amnesia in a patient</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10001949</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Amnesia is a short term memory condition in which memory is disturbed. In simple terms it is the loss of memory.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>amnesia AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE:E12585</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002354</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt:C2867</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0002622</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000483 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000483">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000581"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a movement disorder AE that has an outcome of incoordination</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;incoordination&apos; was mentioned in 261 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>a lack of normal adjustment of muscular action so that the intended movement of the limb or other part is not made smoothly and harmoniously, and does not accurately achieve its objective. If the abnormality is hypermetric, the condition is referred to as ataxia. If it is inclined to weakness, e.g. knuckling at the turn, stumbling, failure to flex limbs properly, or to misdirection as in a proprioceptive deficit, it is called incoordination.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>incoordination AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000484 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000484">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000426"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a speech disorder that has an outcome of voice alteration</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10047681</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>voice alteration AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E13601</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C61043</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000485 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000485">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000064"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a pregnancy AE that is the termination of a pregnancyby the removal or expulsion from the uterus of a fetus or embryo, resulting in or caused by its death.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;abortion&apos;; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 257 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abortion</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10000210</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>abortion AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000486 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000486">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001797"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a psychiatric disorder AE that has an outcome of shock</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>acute stress disorder AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>acute stress reaction AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>mental shock AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10001084</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Mental shock (or shock) is a psychological condition arising in response to a terrifying event. It should not be confused with the unrelated circulatory condition of shock.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>There are two types of shocks. Another is circulatory shock which is physiological with MedDRA ID of 10040560.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>psychological shock AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000487 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000487">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000423"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a skin discoloration AE which has an outcome of purpura</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;purpura&apos;; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 251 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>紫癜</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10037549</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Purpura is the appearance of red or purple discolorations on the skin that do not blanch on applying pressure. They are caused by bleeding underneath the skin. This is common with typhus and can be present with meningitis caused by meningococcal meningitis or septicaemia. Reference: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purpura.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>purpura AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE:E13690</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0000979</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt:C78787</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0034150</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000488 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000488">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000363"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an infection AE that results in detrimental colonization of a host organism by bacteria</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SS</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>bacterial infection AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bacterial_infection</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10060945</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>bacterial infection AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002718</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0004623</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000489 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000489">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000543"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a skin adverse event that has an outcome of skin striae that displays irregular areas of skin that look like bands, stripes, or lines. Striae are seen when a person grows or gains weight rapidly or has certain diseases or conditions.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>According to the Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS), &apos;skin striae&apos;; is an adverse event that was mentioned in 247 VAERS reports (0.2%) during1991-2001 (Reference: PMID: 12825543).</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>stretch marks</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>striae distensae</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:label>skin striae AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001065</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0152459</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000490 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000490">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000364"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a syndrome AE that has an outcome of an acute brain syndrome AE and occurs after a medical intervention. </obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>acute brain syndrome AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000491 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000491">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000582"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a sensory capability AE that has an outcome of coma</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10010071</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Coma is a profound state of unconsciousness. A comatose person cannot be awakened, fails to respond normally to pain or light, does not have sleep-wake cycles, and does not take voluntary actions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>coma AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001259</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0009421</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000492 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000492">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000435"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a muscle adverse event which has an outcome of hyperkinesia, an abnormal increase in muscular activity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10020651</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>hyperkinesia AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0002487</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0424295</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000493 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000493">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000001"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an AE that occurs in cardiovascular system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>cardiovascular disorder AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10007649</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>cardiovascular AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>HPO: HP_0001626</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>SIDER: C0007222</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000494 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000494">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000570"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a nervous system AE which has an outcome of encephalopathy, which is disorder or disease of the brain.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10014625</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>encephalopathy AE</rdfs:label>
