        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000053"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a wheezing AE which has an outcome of stridor, a high pitched wheezing sound resulting from turbulent air flow in the upper airway. It is primarily inspiratory. It can be indicative of serious airway obstruction from severe conditions such as epiglottitis, a foreign body lodged in the airway, or a laryngeal tumor.</obo:IAO_0000115>
