    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002395 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002395">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000443"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Eyelid disorder AE is a eye AE that is a condition specifically affects the eyelid. It can include drooping, twitching, inflammation, paralysis, and growths. Occasional fluttering of one eyelid is normal.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, LW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.healthline.com/health/eyelid-disorders#Overview1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10061130</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>eyelid disorder AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002396 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002396">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001135"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Hepatic steatosis AE is a liver disorder AE than popularly called as ‘fatty liver’ is a pathological aspect of liver, whose specific cells (hepatocytes) are filled with lipids (fats). It is a reversible liver disease: ‘is not still very ill, but cries for help’.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, LW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.bendomd.com/272-hepatic-steatosis-causes-symptoms-treatment.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10019708</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>hepatic steatosis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002397 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002397">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000402"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000442"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>An arthropathy AE is a joint pain AE that has an outcome of arthropahty, which is any disorder of the joints.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is an injury to the abdomen and its signs and symptoms include abdominal pain, tenderness, rigidity, and bruising of the external abdomen.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arthropathy, http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/arthropathy</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Abdominal_trauma</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>腹部损伤</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10003285</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10060924</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">arthropathy AE
</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:label>abdominal injury AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIT: C35760</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002398 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002398">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000651"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A balantis AE is a reproductive system AE that has an outcome of a balantis, which is an infectious or non-infectious inflammatory process that affects the glans penis. Symptoms include redness and pain of the glans penis and foreskin and discharge.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/ency/article/000862.htm, http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balanitis</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10004073</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">balanitis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002399 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002399">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000373"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Pruritus genital AE is a pruritus AE that also called genital itching, Itching in the genital region can result from irritation, allergy, inflammation, infection or cancer. Irritation can occur as a result of exposure to chemicals in soaps, feminine hygiene products, perfumes, lubricants, douches, and creams.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, LW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>genital itching AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.healthgrades.com/symptoms/genital-itching</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10037093</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>pruritus genital AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002400 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002400">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000959"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>cholecystitis AE is an gallbladder enlargement AE that has an outcome of cholecystitis, which is an acute or chronic inflammation involving the gallbladder wall. It may be associated with the presence of gallstones.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cholecystitis, http://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/cholecystitis/basics/definition/con-20034277</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10008612</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cholecystitis AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E11184</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIT: C34465</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C34465</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002401 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002401">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000495"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Chromaturia AE is an urine abnormality AE that has an outcome of chromaturia, which is an abnormal coloration of the urine.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/chromaturia
</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10008796</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">chromaturia AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002402 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002402">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000209"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Chromosome abnormality AE is a genetic AE that has an outcome of chromsome abnormality which is a missing, extra, or irregular protion of chromosomal DNA.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chromosome_abnormality
</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10008815</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">chromosome abnormality AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002403 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002403">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000731"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A coagulopathy AE is a blood disorder AE that has an outcome of coagulopathy, which is a condition in which there is a deviation from or interruption of the normal coagulation properties of the blood.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coagulopathy
</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10009802</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">coagulopathy AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002404 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002404">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Combined immunodeficiency AE is an immune system AE that has an outcome of combined immunodeficiency, which represents a group of rare, sometimes fatal, congenital disorders characterized by little or no immune response.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK22254/
</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10010099</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">combined immunodeficiency AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002405 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002405">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001694"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Hepatic enzyme abnormal AE is a liver related investigation result abnormal AE that the lab test result of hepatic enzyme deviates from its normal value.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10062685</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>hepatic enzyme abnormal AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002406 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002406">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001161"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A coronary artery aneurysm AE is a coronary artery disorder AE that has an outcome of coronary artery aneurysm, which is a coronary dilatation which exceeds the diameter of normal adjacent segments or the diameter of the patient&apos;s largest coronary vessel by 1.5 times.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronary_artery_aneurysm</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9247557</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10011071</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">coronary artery aneurysm AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002407 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002407">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000366"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Injection site atrophy AE is an injection-site AE that muscle atrophy occur in the injection site.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10022048</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>injection site atrophy AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002408 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002408">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001474"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cutaneous tuberculosis AE is a tuberculosis AE that has an outcome of cutaneous tuberculosis, which is an invasion of the skin by Mycobacterium tuberculosis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>KM, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.dermnetnz.org/bacterial/tuberculosis.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10011684</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cutaneous tuberculosis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002409 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002409">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000378"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Breath sounds abnormal AE is a respiratory system AE that is characterized by abnormal breath sound, it can indicate fluid in the lungs or asthma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, LW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.healthline.com/health/breath-sounds#Overview1</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10064780</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>breath sounds abnormal AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002410 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002410">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000543"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Skin abrasion AE is a skin AE that is a wound caused by superficial damage to the skin, no deeper than the epidermis.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abrasion_%28medical%29</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10064990</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>skin abrasion AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002411 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002411">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000514"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Trigeminal neuralgia AE is a neuralgia AE that is a neuropathic disorder characterized by episodes of intense pain in the face, originating from the trigeminal nerve. The clinical association between TN and hemifacial spasm is the so-called tic douloureux.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>Fothergill&apos;s disease AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>prosopalgia AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trigeminal_neuralgia</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10044652</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>trigeminal neuralgia AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002412 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002412">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000041"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Face injury AE is an injury AE that injury occurs in the face.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10050392</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>face injury AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002413 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002413">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000435"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Muscle contrature AE is a muscle AE that can occur for many reasons, such as paralysis, muscular atrophy, and forms of muscular dystrophy. Fundamentally, the muscle and its tendons shorten, resulting in reduced flexibility.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muscle_contracture</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10062575</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>muscle contrature AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002414 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002414">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0004344"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A palsy AE that has a symmetric limitation of the movements of both eyes in the same direction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://one.aao.org/bcscsnippetdetail.aspx?id=f5a77965-de2a-4fb0-82fb-5f4089671ad6</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10056696</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>gaze palsy AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002415 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002415">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002414"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Conjugate gaze palsy AE is a gaze palsy AE that is a disorder affecting the ability to move both eyes in the same direction. These palsies can affect gaze in a horizontal, upward, or downward direction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conjugate_gaze_palsy</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label>conjugate gaze palsy AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002416 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002416">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002414"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Horizontal gaze palsy AE is a gaze palsy AE that is the paresis of conjugate eye movements.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horizontal_gaze_palsy</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label>horizontal gaze palsy AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002417 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002417">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavioral and neurological AE that refers to rigid body movements and chronic abnormal positions of the body. This symptom is not the same as showing poor posture or slumping over. Rather, it is often the result of a serious spinal cord or brain injury.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.healthline.com/symptom/posture-abnormal</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10036436</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>posture abnormal AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002418 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002418">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000580"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavioral and neurological AE that shows the body becomes entire rigid and uncontrolled jerking. They may last mere seconds, or continue for several minutes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10051171</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>tonic clonic movements AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002419 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002419">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002395"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Eyelid ptosis AE is an eye disorder AE that is a drooping or falling of the upper or lower eyelid.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, LW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptosis_%28eyelid%29</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10015995</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>eyelid ptosis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002420 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002420">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000205"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Facial paresis AE is a paresis AE that is a common problem that involves the paralysis of any structures innervated by the facial nerve.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>facial nerve paralysis AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facial_nerve_paralysis</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10051267</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>facial paresis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002421 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002421">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000082"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Menstrual disorder AE is an abnormal condition in a woman&apos;s menstrual cycle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menstrual_disorder</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10027327</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <dc:creator>JX, YH</dc:creator>
        <rdfs:label>menstrual disorder AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002422 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002422">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000546"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Fluid retention AE is an abnormal fluid regulation AE that is excess fluid that collects in the tissues in your body. Most commonly, fluid retention is marked by swelling of your feet and lower legs, but swelling could also occur in your arms, hands, face, or other areas of the body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.healthgrades.com/symptoms/fluid-retention</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10016807</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>fluid retention AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002423 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002423">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000914"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Emotional distress AE is a emotional disorder AE that is a Mental distress or anxiety suffered as a response to a sudden, severe, and saddening experience.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emotional_distress</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10049119</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>emotional distress AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002424 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002424">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000558"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Encephalitis AE is a nervous system AE that is an acute inflammation of the brain.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encephalitis</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10014581</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>encephalitis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002425 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002425">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001797"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a psychiatric disorder AE that is a category of mental health disorders that primarily affect learning, memory, perception, and problem solving, and include amnesia, dementia, and delirium.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognitive_disorder</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10057668</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>cognitive disorder AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002426 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002426">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000426"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Incoherent AE is a speech disorder AE that shows unable to express one&apos;s thoughts or ideas in an orderly, intelligible manner.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/incoherent</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10021630</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>incoherent AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002427 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002427">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000063"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Exercise tolerance decreased AE is a systematic AE that shows exercise tolerance decreased. The exercise tolerance refers to the exercise capacity of an individual as measured by their ability to endure exercise and/or the maximum work load achieved during the exercise period.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://copd.about.com/od/glossaryofcopdterms/g/activitytoleran.htm</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10051301</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>exercise tolerance decreased AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002428 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002428">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002569"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a burn AE that is a type of burn resulted from making contact with heated objects, such as boiling water, steam, hot cooking oil, fire, and hot objects.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, LW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermal_burn</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10053615</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>thermal burn AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002429 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002429">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001797"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a psychiatric disorder AE that describes a wide array of experiences from mild detachment from immediate surroundings to more severe detachment from physical and emotional experience.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dissociation_%28psychology%29</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10013457</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>dissociation AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002431 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002431">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000063"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mucous membrane disorder AE is a systematic AE that the diseases occur in mucous membrane, which is a lining of mostly endodermal origin.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mucous_membrane</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10028133</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>mucous membrane disorder AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002432 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002432">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000169"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a polyneuropathy AE that arises when the myelin sheaths around nerve cells are damaged. Myelin, the insulating layer of tissue that surrounds nerve cells, helps ensure that signals from the brain are rapidly transmitted to the proper places in the body. When myelin is damaged or destroyed, it can lead to problems with communication between the brain and the body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.healthgrades.com/conditions/chronic-inflammatory-demyelinating-polyneuropathy</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10061811</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>demyelinating polyneuropathy AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002433 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002433">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000364"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a syndrome AE that results in increased pressure in a muscle compartment which can lead to nerve damage and impaired blood flow.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>URL: http://www.nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/ency/article/001224.htm</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10010121</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Thick layers of tissue, called fascia, separate groups of muscles in the arms and legs from each other. Inside each layer of fascia is a confined space, called a compartment. The compartment includes the muscle tissue, nerves, and blood vessels.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">compartment syndrome AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002434 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002434">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002475"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Therapeutic response decreased is found among people who take Cialis, especially for people who are male, 60+ old, have been taking the drug for &lt; 1 month, also take medication Aspirin, and have Erection problems.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, LW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.ehealthme.com/ds/cialis/therapeutic+response+decreased</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10043414</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>therapeutic response decreased</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002436 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002436">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000579"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a seizure AE that resutls in impariment of awareness and involuntary but coordinated and repeated movements.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, SJ </obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.webmd.com/epilepsy/guide/types-of-seizures-their-symptoms?page=2</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10010145</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">complex partial seizure AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002437 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002437">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000476"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Autoimmune disorder AE is an immune system AE that arises from an abnormal immune response of the body against substances and tissues normally present in the body (autoimmunity).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autoimmune_disease</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10061664</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>autoimmune disorder AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E11258</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C2889</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002438 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002438">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000427"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a hemorrhage AE that has an outcome of bleeding into the pons or mesencephalon.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/brainstem+hemorrhage</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10006146</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>brain stem hemorrhage AE is often secondary to brainstem distortion due to rapidly expanding intracranail lessions.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">brainstem hemorrhage AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002439 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002439">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002421"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Menstruation irregular AE is a endocrine system AE that is an abnormal variation in length of menstrual cycles in a female.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>irregular menstruation AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irregular_menstruation</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10022992</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10027339</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>menstruation irregular AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE: E13125</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt: C35219</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002440 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002440">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000579"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Generalised tonic-clonic seizure AE is a seizure AE that is a type of generalized seizure that affects the entire brain. Tonic–clonic seizures are the seizure type most commonly associated with epilepsy and seizures in general, though it is a misconception that they are the only type.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonic%E2%80%93clonic_seizure</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10018100</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>generalised tonic-clonic seizure AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002441 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002441">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001797"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a psychiatric disorder AE that an involuntary flexion or extension of the arms and legs, indicating severe brain injury.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abnormal_posturing</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10036437</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>posturing AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002443 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002443">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000570"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Demyelination AE is a nervous system AE that is any disease of the nervous system in which the myelin sheath of neurons is damaged.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demyelinating_disease</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10012305</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>demyelination AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002444 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002444">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001605"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Gram stain negative AE is a microbiology and serology investigation result abnormal AE that has an outcome of detection of gram-negative bacteria.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gram-negative_bacteria</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10018656</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>gram stain negative AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002445 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002445">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000293"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Red blood cells CSF positive AE is a CSF test result abnormal AE that has an outcome of CSF red blood cells count positive.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10038173</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>red blood cells CSF positive AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002446 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002446">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000293"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>CSF white blood cell count increased AE is a CSF test result abnormal AE that has an outcome of CSF white blood cell count increased.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10053805</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>CSF white blood cell count increased AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002447 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002447">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000675"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Influenza A virus test positive AE is a influenza virus test positive AE that has an outcome of positive result in an influenza A virus test.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10070215</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>influenza A virus test positive AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002448 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002448">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001643"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a behavior and neurological test abnormal AE that shows a abnormal result of nerve conduction study (NCS). NCS is a medical diagnostic test commonly used to evaluate the function, especially the ability of electrical conduction, of the motor and sensory nerves of the human body.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nerve_conduction_study</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10029175</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>nerve conduction study abnormal AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002449 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002449">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000197"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Myocardial necrosis AE is a cardiac disorder AE that shows death of the cells of an area of the heart muscle (myocardium) as a result of oxygen deprivation, which in turn is caused by obstruction of the blood supply.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>JX, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>URL: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/myocardial+necrosis</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10028602</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>myocardial necrosis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002450 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002450">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001790"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a brainstem infarction AE is a stroke AE that occurs when blood cannot flow to the brainstem, when oxygen cannot get to an area of the brain, tissue in that area may be damaged.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>brainstem stroke</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain_stem_stroke_syndrome</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.drugs.com/cg/brain-stem-infarction.html
</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10006147</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>A person may have vertigo, dizziness and severe imbalance without the hallmark of most strokes – weakness on one side of the body. But dizziness alone is not a sign of stroke. Brain stem stroke can also cause diplopia, slurred speech and decreased level of consciousness.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">brainstem infarction AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002451 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002451">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000434"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a lung disorder AE that occurs when the noises produced by the structures of the lungs during breathing are decreased or absent.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117> SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.nlm.nih.gov/medlineplus/ency/article/007535.htm</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10006333</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>Absent or decreased breath sounds can indicate air or fluid around the lungs, increased thickness of chest wall, over-inflation of part of the lungs, or reduced airflow to part of the lungs.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">breath sounds decreased AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002452 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002452">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000364"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a syndrome AE that is characterised by abnormal electrocardiogram (ECG) findings and an increased risk of sudden cardiac death.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>sudden adult death syndrome (SADS)</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brugada_syndrome</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10059027</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Brugada syndrome AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002453 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002453">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000374"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Buttock pain AE is a pain AE that  is a common problem in the butt, it can be due to  bursitis, bruising, piriformis syndrome, and shingles,or due to more serious diseases with long-term consequences, such as cancer, arthritis of the sacroiliac joints, and herniated disc with sciatica.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH, MW</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>Butt Pain </obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB:http://www.medicinenet.com/buttock_pain/symptoms.htm</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10048677</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">buttock pain AE</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>CTCAE:E12396</rdfs:seeAlso>
        <rdfs:seeAlso>NCIt:C78228</rdfs:seeAlso>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002454 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002454">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000439"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a digestive system AE with an outcome of small white calcium lumps forming under the skin that may leak a chalky white fluid. These lumps are formed becuase of too much calcium in the diet.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://www.sclero.org/medical/symptoms/skin/calcinosis.html</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10006938</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>These most commonly occur on the hands, or near joints such as elbows or knees, although they may appear anywhere. Calcinosis may range from one very tiny deposit, to large (and often painful) clusters.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">calcinosis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002455 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002455">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000363"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>an infection adverse event that caused by a species of the yeast Candida.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/candidiasis</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10007152</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>This is a common cause of vaginal infections in women. Also, Candida may cause mouth infections in people with reduced immune function, or in patients taking certain antibiotics. Candida can be found in virtually all normal people but causes problems in only a fraction.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">candidiasis AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002456 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002456">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001664"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>a hematology investigation result abnormal AE that occurs when the cardaic enzymes and proteins leak out of damaged heart muscle cells, and their levels in the bloodstream rise.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>URL: http://www.webmd.com/heart-disease/cardiac-enzyme-studies</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10007548</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:comment>cardiac enzymes increased AE may indicate that the heart muscle is injured, such as from a heart attack.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cardiac enzymes increased AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002457 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002457">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000779"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Acute decompensated heart failure AE is a cardiovascular disorder AE that shows  a worsening of the symptoms, typically shortness of breath (dyspnea), edema, and fatigue, in a patient with existing heart disease.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>Cardiac Failure Acute</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>WEB: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acute_decompensated_heart_failure</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10007556</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10064653</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">acute decompensated heart failure AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002459 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002459">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000084"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Cardiac murmur AE  is a cardiac disorder AE that is characterised by abnormal sounds during the heartbeat cycle — such as whooshing or swishing — made by turbulent blood in or near the heart.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>SJ, YH</obo:IAO_0000117>
