        <obo:IAO_0000115>an antibody test abnormal AE that shows positive antinuclear antibody, which often attack a person&apos;s own cell nucleus.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>YH, KY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>ANA test abnormal AE</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>URL: http://www.mayoclinic.org/tests-procedures/ana-test/basics/definition/prc-20014566</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:comment>In most cases, a positive ANA test indicates that your immune system has launched a misdirected attack on your own tissue — in other words, an autoimmune reaction. But some people have positive ANA tests even when they&apos;re healthy.
Ref: http://www.mayoclinic.org/tests-procedures/ana-test/basics/definition/prc-20014566</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">antinuclear antibody positive AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


