        <obo:OAE_0004334>10044299</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>tracheal ulcer AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008644 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008644">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000378"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is a condition or incident where the cartilage that keeps the airway (trachea) open is soft such that the trachea partly collapses especially during increased airflow.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Tracheomalacia</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>气管软化</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10056397</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>tracheomalacia AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008645 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008645">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001373"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is a surgical procedure infection which consists of making an incision (cut) on the anterior aspect (front) of the neck and opening a direct airway through an incision in the trachea (windpipe) .</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Tracheotomy</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>气管切开感染</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10066335</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>tracheostomy infection AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008646 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008646">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002217"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is a surgical procedure which consists of making an incision (cut) on the anterior aspect (front) of the neck and opening a direct airway through an incision in the trachea (windpipe) and the surgical procedure results are malfunction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Tracheotomy</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>气管切开术功能障碍</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10044322</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>tracheostomy malfunction AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008647 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008647">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000337"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is a condition in which there is compression of the nerves, arteries, or veins in the passageway from the lower neck to the armpit.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Thoracic_outlet_syndrome</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>胸廓出口综合征</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10048627</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>thoracic outlet syndrome AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008648 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008648">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0003445"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is a marker of bone fragility on the thoracic and is associated with a downward spiral of recurrent fractures known as the vertebral fracture cascade.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26363627/</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>胸椎骨折</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10049948</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>thoracic vertebral fracture AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008649 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008649">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0002217"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is any damage or abnormal change in the throat  tissue of an organism, usually caused by disease or trauma.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Lesion</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>喉咙病变</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10054830</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>throat lesion AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008650 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008650">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000377"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is a headache that is severe and has a sudden onset and  is defined as a severe headache that takes seconds to minutes to reach maximum intensity.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Thunderclap_headache</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <obo:OAE_0001849>霹雳性头痛</obo:OAE_0001849>
        <obo:OAE_0004334>10075481</obo:OAE_0004334>
        <rdfs:label>thunderclap headache AE</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008651 -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0008651">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0001164"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>This is an AE which is a tumor originating from the epithelial cells of the thymus that is considered a rare malignancy.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>QY, JX, HY</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://en.volupedia.org/wiki/Thymoma</obo:IAO_0000119>
